---
source: crates/zeff-engine/tests/expressions.rs
expression: all
---
## text_in_arithmetic (exit 1)
error[Z0215]: `+` does not apply to text
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | "a" + "b"
  | ^^^^^^^^^ text in arithmetic
  |
  = help: `join` puts texts together and `format` builds text from values (release 0.5.0); a number in text converts with `to(x, Float)`

## bool_in_arithmetic (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `+` needs numbers, but one side is a Bool
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | true + 1
  | ^^^^^^^^ a Bool
  |
  = help: Bool is not a number; `to(x, Int)` turns true and false into 1 and 0

## negating_text (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `-` needs a number, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:7
  |
2 | print(-t)
  |       ^^ a Str
  |
  = help: only an Int or a Float can be negated

## not_on_a_number (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `!` needs a Bool, but this is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | !3
  | ^^ an Int
  |
  = help: `!` negates true, false and NA; compare a number first, as in `!(x > 0)`

## logic_on_numbers (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `&&` needs two Bools, but one side is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | 1 && 2
  | ^^^^^^ an Int
  |
  = help: `&&` and `||` combine comparisons, as in `age > 18 && female`

## comparing_different_types (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `==` compares values of one type, but these are an Int and a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | 1 == "1"
  | ^^^^^^^^ different types
  |
  = help: Int and Float compare as numbers; text compares with text and Bool with Bool

## ordering_a_bool_with_a_number (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `<` compares values of one type, but these are a Bool and an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | true < 2
  | ^^^^^^^^ different types
  |
  = help: Int and Float compare as numbers; text compares with text and Bool with Bool

## comparing_lists (exit 1)
error[Z0208]: `==` is not defined for a List<Int>
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | [1] == [1]
  | ^^^^^^^^^^ compared here
  |
  = help: comparison is for single values: numbers, text, Bool, dates and NA; compare the items of a list one by one

## interaction_outside_a_formula (exit 1)
error[Z0306]: `:` is an interaction and belongs in a formula
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | 2 : 3
  | ^^^^^ not in a formula
  |
  = help: write `a:b` inside a formula or a `fe:` argument; multiplication is `*`

## range_of_floats (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `..` needs two Ints, but one end is a Float
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | 1.5..3
  | ^^^^^^ a Float
  |
  = help: a range runs from one whole number to another: `2..5`

## indexing_a_number (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `[ ]` indexes a list or a mapping, not an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | 3[1]
  | ^^^^ an Int
  |
  = help: `xs[2]` takes the second item of a list; `m[k]` looks a key up in a mapping

## indexing_a_list_with_text (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: a list is indexed by an Int, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:8
  |
1 | [1, 2]["a"]
  |        ^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: positions count from 1: `xs[1]` is the first item

## mapping_key_of_the_wrong_type (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: this mapping's keys are an Int, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:12
  |
1 | [1 => "a"]["x"]
  |            ^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: look a mapping up by a key of its own type

## mixed_mapping_keys (exit 1)
error[Z0214]: a mapping has one key type: this one has an Int and a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:12
  |
1 | [1 => "a", "b" => "c"]
  |            ^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: give every entry the same kinds of key and value

## mixed_mapping_values (exit 1)
error[Z0214]: a mapping has one value type: this one has a Str and an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:17
  |
1 | [1 => "a", 2 => 3]
  |                 ^ an Int
  |
  = help: give every entry the same kinds of key and value

## duplicate_mapping_key (exit 1)
error[Z0222]: a mapping's keys are unique, but this key is written twice
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:12
  |
1 | [1 => "a", 1 => "b"]
  |  - the first time
  |            ^ the second time
  |
  = help: keep one entry for the key

## duplicate_key_at_run_time (exit 1)
error[Z0222]: a mapping's keys are unique, but this key appears twice
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:26
  |
2 | [1 => "a", 1 + 1 => "b", k => "c"]
  |                          ^ `2` again
  |
  = help: keep one entry for the key

## missing_record_field (exit 1)
error[Z0209]: the record has no field `b`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:15
  |
1 | {a: 1, bb: 2}.b
  |               ^ its fields are a, bb
  |
  = help: did you mean `a`?

## field_of_a_number (exit 1)
warning[W0101]: `n` hides the function `data::n`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:5
  |
1 | let n = 3
  |     ^ a binding with a built-in name
  |
  = help: the function is still reachable as `data::n`; a different name avoids the confusion
error[Z0213]: `.a` reads a record field, but this is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | n.a
  | ^^^ an Int
  |
  = help: a method call has parentheses: `.a()`

## nothing_in_arithmetic (exit 1)
error[Z0206]: this gives no value, so it cannot be used in an expression
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | print(1) + 1
  | ^^^^^^^^ its type is Nothing
  |
  = help: `print` and the other statements that print or warn return nothing; use the value they were given

## int_overflow (exit 1)
error[Z0211]: Int overflow: 9223372036854775807 + 1 does not fit in 64 bits
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | 9223372036854775807 + 1
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the operation
  |
  = help: Ints are 64-bit; a Float (`1.0 * x`) holds larger magnitudes with 53 bits of precision

## index_outside (exit 1)
error[Z0207]: index 4 is outside 1..3
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | [1, 2, 3][4]
  |           ^ the list has 3 items
  |
  = help: positions count from 1 to the list's length

